{
  "description": [
    "Vauchi known-answer vectors, produced by vauchi-core's shipped functions.",
    "All byte strings are lower-case hex. KDF: HKDF-SHA256 (RFC 5869); AEAD: XChaCha20-Poly1305 in the 0x02/0x03 tagged format; curves: X25519 and Ed25519.",
    "identity: Ed25519 key from the master seed; X25519 exchange key from HKDF(seed, info); per-device id and exchange key from HKDF(seed, info || index as little-endian u32).",
    "x3dh: shared_key = HKDF(salt = none, ikm = DH1 || DH2, info) with DH1 = X25519(initiator static, responder static) and DH2 = X25519(initiator ephemeral, responder static), as X3DH::respond computes it.",
    "ratchet: (root_key || send_chain_key_0) = HKDF(salt = x3dh_secret, ikm = DH(initiator dh, responder dh), root_info, 64 bytes); message_key_0 = HKDF(chain key, message_key_info); send_chain_key_1 = HKDF(chain key, chain_key_info). message.ciphertext encrypts pad(plaintext) with message_key_0 and the 44-byte header as associated data; the nonce and the padding bytes are random, so only decryption is reproducible.",
    "mailbox_tokens: token = HKDF(ikm, info || recipient key [|| device id] || day_epoch as big-endian u64) with ikm the shared key (contact tokens) or the master seed (device-sync token).",
    "backup: 0x03 || salt(16) || XChaCha20-Poly1305(key, zlib(json)); key = HKDF-expand(HKDF-extract(none, Argon2id(password, salt)), hkdf_info, 32). This is the legacy format the importer still accepts.",
    "backup_v6: header = 0x06 || salt(16); file = header || XChaCha20-Poly1305(key, zlib(json), associated data = header) in the 0x03 tagged format; key = HKDF-expand(HKDF-extract(none, Argon2id(password, salt)), hkdf_info, 32). This is the format the app exports today; the nonce is random, so only decryption is reproducible."
  ],
